From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c <a@b>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 11:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: keep the renderer alive on game launch under
 gamescope

Launching any game from the UI killed EmulationStation outright: black
screen, session restart, no game. Caught under gdb on the DMG - ES logs
"Interrupt signal SIGSEGV received" from its own handler and exits, so
the kernel never writes a core and the fault has to be trapped before
that handler sees it:

  #0  wl_proxy_marshal_flags () from /usr/lib/libwayland-client.so.0
  #1  ?? () from /usr/lib/libSDL2-2.0.so.0
  #2  ?? () from /usr/lib/libSDL2-2.0.so.0
  #3..#10 emulationstation
  #11 main ()

HideWindow defaults to true on everything that is not x86, and it makes
FileData::launchGame() call Window::deinit(true) before every launch,
which runs Renderer::deinit() and tears the SDL2 window down, then
rebuilds it on return. ROCKNIX builds SDL2 with VIDEO_X11=OFF, so in
this session SDL2 is a native Wayland client talking to gamescope: the
teardown leaves a dangling proxy and the next wl_proxy_marshal_flags()
runs on freed memory. The session log shows the matching
"[Gamescope WSI] Destroying swapchain" immediately before each crash.

x86 has always defaulted this to false, so the no-teardown path is the
well-travelled one rather than an experiment. Take it whenever a
gamescope session is what we are running inside: Window::deinit(false)
then only drops resources and Window::init(false) calls
Renderer::activateWindow(), so no window is destroyed and SDL2 has
nothing to dangle.

Keyed on GAMESCOPE_WAYLAND_DISPLAY, which the session exports as part of
its handshake, so this stays inert on sway and weston builds.

Verified on the AYANEO Pocket DMG: ES now launches RetroArch from the UI
and survives the return, with the session restart counter still at zero,
where the same action crashed ES every time before. Frame pacing under
load is unaffected - "atomic commit failed" stays at 0.
---
 es-core/src/Settings.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/es-core/src/Settings.cpp b/es-core/src/Settings.cpp
--- a/es-core/src/Settings.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/Settings.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <pugixml/src/pugixml.hpp>
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <vector>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include "utils/StringUtil.h"
 #include "Paths.h"
 #include "../es-app/src/ApiSystem.h"
@@ -352,7 +353,13 @@
 #if defined(_WIN32) || defined(X86) || defined(X86_64)
 	mBoolMap["HideWindow"] = false;
 #else
-	mBoolMap["HideWindow"] = true;
+	// Under a gamescope session this has to be false, exactly as on x86.
+	// With it true, launchGame() calls Window::deinit(true) every time, which
+	// runs Renderer::deinit() and tears down the SDL2 window. SDL2 here is a
+	// native Wayland client (VIDEO_X11=OFF), so the teardown leaves a dangling
+	// proxy and the next wl_proxy_marshal_flags() segfaults inside
+	// libwayland-client: ES dies and the user gets a black screen, not a game.
+	mBoolMap["HideWindow"] = (getenv("GAMESCOPE_WAYLAND_DISPLAY") == nullptr);
 #endif
 
 	mBoolMap["HideWindowFullReinit"] = false;
